            "id": "PR_kwDOErHI988AAAABH0aNdg",
            "number": 1585,
            "title": "fix(static): normalize indexNames joining to prevent double slash at root",
            "body": "Resolves #1584\n\n### Description\n\nIn `src/utils/static.ts`, `idSearchPaths` currently builds candidate asset IDs with `${id}${suffix}`.\n\nBecause `originalId` for root `GET /` is `\"/\"`:\n- Default `indexNames: [\"/index.html\"]`: Requesting root `GET /` produces candidate ID `\"//index.html\"` (an invalid double-slash path that fails lookups against canonical asset maps or storage systems).\n- Relative `indexNames: [\"index.html\"]`: Requesting a subfolder like `GET /docs` produces `\"/docsindex.html\"` (missing the path separator).\n\nThis patch normalizes the join boundary in `idSearchPaths` so that:\n- Any leading slashes on index names are stripped before joining.\n- If `id` is `\"/\"`, the root index becomes `\"/index.html\"`.\n- If `id` is a subpath like `\"/docs\"`, the directory index becomes `\"/docs/index.html\"`.\n\n### Checklist\n- [x] Code passes `pnpm lint`\n- [x] Code passes `pnpm test`\n- [x] Automated tests added covering root `/`, subpaths, and both leading/non-leading slash `indexNames`\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n* **Bug Fixes**\n  * Fixed static index-file resolution when the configured index path begins with `/`, including requests to the site root and subdirectories with or without a trailing slash.\n  * Static file requests can resolve `/about` to `/about.html` when `.html` is configured as an extension fallback.\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->",
